%Lyrics - Larksong of Second Breakfast

%Almost hidden
%West of Bree-land
%Green Hill Country
%Brandywine River

%Never cold there
%Sun's up in the sky
%Soft and gentle rains come
%To grow the pipe-weed high

%Great East Road, take me home
%To the place I belong
%Little Delving, in the Shire
%Take me home, Great East Road

%All my memories
%Gather round them:
%Bird and Baby, Hobbiton-Bywater
%Stock and Scary
%Overhill nearby
%The Marish in the moonshine
%Golden fields of rye

%Great East Road, take me home
%To the place I belong
%A cozy burrow by the fire
%Take me home, Great East Road

%I hear the laughter in the evenings at the Green Dragon
%A coney pie reminds me of my home far away
%Riding down the road I hear my Gaffer saying,
%"Should have been home yesterday, yesterday . . ."

%Great East Road, take me home
%To the place I belong
%Little Delving, in the Shire
%Take me home, Great East Road

%Great East Road, take me home
%To the place I belong
%Little Delving, in the Shire
%Take me home, Great East Road
%Take me home, Great East Road
%Take me home, Great East Road

